bitcoind-virtual-mainnet
Copyright (c) 2026 Andrzej Broński

This project ports no third-party source of its own. It distributes a patch
against Bitcoin Core (MIT), applied at build time to the `bitcoind` package from
nixpkgs; Bitcoin Core is neither vendored nor redistributed here. The patch
modifies src/kernel/chainparams.cpp and src/pow.cpp so that the regtest network
carries mainnet's genesis hash, address prefixes and p2p magic.

The resulting binary is a TEST HARNESS. Because it answers with mainnet's
genesis and speaks mainnet's p2p magic, it is wire-compatible with the real
Bitcoin network and must never be allowed to reach it. See the README.
